## DESCRIPTION
## Find the solution to a system of 2 equations and 2 variables.  The solution to this
## system does not exist.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear Algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of Linear Equations)
## DBsection(Systems with 2 variables)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('linear system', '2 by 2', 'no solution')

# updated on 2022.10.29

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'contextFraction.pl',
    'MatrixReduce.pl'
);

Context('Numeric')->variables->add(y => 'Real');
Context()->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

do {
    $A = Matrix([
        [ non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5) ],
        [ non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5) ],
    ]);
} while ($A->det != 0) && $A->row(1) != $A->row(2);

$x = Matrix([ [ random(-4, 4) ], [ random(-4, 4) ] ]);
$b = $A * $x;
# create a b-vector such that there will not be a solution.
$b = Matrix([
    [ $b->element(1, 1) ], [ $b->element(2, 1) + non_zero_random(1, 4) ] ]);

$line1 = Formula($A->element(1, 1) . 'x+' . $A->element(1, 2) . 'y')->reduce;
$line2 = Formula($A->element(2, 1) . 'x+' . $A->element(2, 2) . 'y')->reduce;

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['There is no solution to the linear system'],
        ['There are an infinite number of solutions to the linear system.'],
        [
            'There is a single solution to the linear system in the form %s',
            ''
        ]
    ],
    0
);

BEGIN_PGML
Solve the follow linear system using the Gauss-Jordon method:

[```
\begin{aligned}
[$line1] & = [@ $b->element(1,1) @] \\
[$line2] & = [@ $b->element(2,1) @]
\end{aligned}
```]

Select the following result about the solution to this linear system.

[____]{$rma}

If there is a solution, write it as a vector like <1,2,3> or using the free variable [`t`] if needed. 
END_PGML

Context('Fraction');    # for fraction arithmetic

# augmented matrix to be reduced
$aug = Matrix([
    [ $A->element(1, 1), $A->element(1, 2), $b->element(1, 1) ],
    [ $A->element(2, 1), $A->element(2, 2), $b->element(2, 1) ]
]);

$aug_red = rref($aug);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

First, start with the augmented coefficient matrix or
[``` [$aug] ```]

and then perform Gauss-Jordon reduction to get 
[``` [$aug_red] ```]

Since the second row corresponds to the equation [` 0 = [$aug_red->element(2,3)] `], 
this has no solution.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
COMMENT('There is no solution to this system.');
ENDDOCUMENT();
